e digits, or significant Republican outside spending in the final weeks, would narrow this.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Dina Titus seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans Democratic by about two points, in an environment currently favoring her party. She won renomination in June and faces state senator Carrie Buck, who has raised a competitive sum but trails badly on cash on hand, $654,000 to $1.34 million. Minor independent candidates are on the ballot but are not factors.\n\nForecasters broadly rate the race Likely D or better, with two calling it Safe D and one Lean D. Prediction markets put Titus's chances in the low-to-mid 90s. With no public general-election polling available, the forecast leans on fundamentals, ratings, and markets, all of which point to a Titus win by roughly a dozen points, though the absence of polling keeps uncertainty elevated.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}]}